{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head b3c4b1147e7769b21e97dc9486a99598bef676d6, tree 33acbe056c20f26b8789dbcd7e40a6de25bdcbc7, on builder/nf6-nf8-on-c3-sh1-source-20261115, all 88 artifacts, for request 3794d78d under my promise e8f14095 and standing da772676. This verdict names all five implementations: NF-6 (request 9ca61777, promise 60680427, report 90e1323a, primary), NF-8 (request 0a0da4ca, promise d549e079, report 128ad074), FH-2 (request efdebe55, promise 8d8c4c3f, report 612a1570), SD-1 (request 905e4ecd, promise 8a788b09, report f310f737) and LC-2 (request 46072a19, promise d59fe799, report 08f82ff7). `gs review --prepare` resolved all five bindings and reports at this head, with each request closing on the sealed receipt. I read the head from the shared object store.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- NF-6. `packages/mcp/src/index.ts` drops the 16 value and 12 type custody aliases. `packages/mcp/src/node.ts` drops the seven Node aliases, and `sqlite-custody.ts` drops `OUTCOMES_INLINE`, which MCP's `export *` would otherwise have kept alive. No tracked file at the head imports any of those names from `@generalbusiness/dap-mcp` or its `/node` entry. Each consumer now imports from `@generalbusiness/dap-client` or `/node`. The MCP index seal row changes to 95ab1f1d…, the value of the reviewed `sourceSeal` calculation in act b1b15c5d.\n- NF-8. The new case in `packages/client/test/custody.test.ts` starts a real second process on the same file store. That process enters `store.exclusive` and holds the lease until it reads `release` on stdin. The parent's send persists `sent`, reaches the unchanged dispatch fence and gets `locked`. The case then asserts one build, no delivery, one signing, no outcome and the same envelope bytes. A new `Custody` on the same store sends again with a builder that throws if called. The case asserts that the delivery receives the kept bytes exactly once, and that a terminal repeat delivers nothing. The case changes no production lease, lock or custody code. `RETIRED_REQUEST` drops only \"Nothing was sent.\", which answers my review b6e9f538.\n- FH-2. `scripts/pre-commit.mjs` lists the staged non-deleted paths first. It requires Prettier and runs the formatter only when a staged path is selected JSON. It runs the helper check only when a staged path matches the helper pathspecs. `scripts/shared-helper-selection.mjs` now owns those pathspecs and the filter, and `check-shared-helpers.mjs` imports the same module, so the hook and the gate select the same files. The hook, `format-json.mjs`, the selection module and `check-commit-messages.mjs` import only `node:` modules at load, so a checkout without `node_modules` can commit a note. The refusal order and the messages are unchanged.\n- SD-1. Four registrations take `scaleDeadline` with their old bases: the archive producer at 30,000 ms, the archive command at 100,000 ms, G15 at 275,000 ms and raw-proof residency at 162,000 ms. With no factor set, `scaleDeadline` returns the base, so Native defaults do not change. `scripts/scale-deadline-registrations.mjs` parses each Scale owner and its factories without importing them. It refuses unknown forms, registrations inside initializers and a shadowed `scaleDeadline`. The new case in `scale-selection.test.mjs` requires every fixed registration to match a listed exception, and each owner's count to equal `scopeScaleCaseCounts`. Its source-string faults show that an added fixed case, a hidden registration and a shadowed helper each fail.\n- LC-2. The two 0.3.0 packets have SHA-256 84f8e5f8… (Lending) and 81b59b8c… (Counter), the values in signing END 37119ff2. The two `dap-lending` trust rows name releases 51f8afe2… and 0b3e5038… with the publisher key of that END. The reproduction owner reads each packet under its trusted release, checks the publisher and host, and requires each trust row to match exactly one committed packet. The 0.2.0 packets and their trust rows are gone. `format-json.mjs` names the 0.3.0 packets as canonical protocol packets.\n- The 0.4.0 raise. Lending and Counter each change the version in `package.ts` and `dap.application.json`, plus the presentation identifier in `release-identifiers.json`. Entry, definitions and semantic identifiers stay exact, as END 3f54a4e6 measured. The \"Raise the version\" assertion is unchanged. It compares a packet with current source only when their versions are equal, so it skips both packets at this head. The LC-2 note's control shows that it fails when the versions are equal and the tuple differs.\n- The five notes, including the dated merges, the STOP at a7f24240 that led to decision c168799e, the controls and the withheld browser files.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main c6711b53 is an ancestor. The 88 artifacts name the head, no path repeats, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only c6711b53 b3c4b114`, deletions included. From 27e01659 to the head only the four notes change.\n- Gate. `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-15-nf6-nf8-fh2-sd1-lc2-full-gate-attempt1/gate.log` has SHA-256 44a98658…, and `result.json` has 2586c1ea…, as END 9d48f8f0 states. The log names head 27e01659 and tree 66ccd762 with 0 changed files. Plain passed 4858 with 1 skipped, and Native passed 1158 with 2 skipped. Scope-scale ran 13 observed modules, including G15 at 77.3 s and raw-proof residency at 54.9 s. Its last line is \"gate passed\". The 1,282,098 ms Native wall includes Scale.\n- Browser. END 9264fbca records 12 local macOS commands passing at 27e01659. No Linux Page or Card run is claimed.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 17 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The custody names have one home in the client, and MCP keeps only its own names and the NF-4 reader aliases. The hook and the gate take their file selection from one module each. One inventory module now finds every Scale deadline, and the guard fails on any fixed deadline that the list does not name. The signed packets are immutable, and current source moves to 0.4.0 under rule 163de663.\n\nSecurity: no finding. Contention can now cost a CLI or MCP send one `locked` answer, but the envelope stays kept and the next send delivers the same bytes once, with no second signing. The trust rows name only the two signed releases under the existing publisher key, and the reader refuses a packet under a wrong release. The FH-2 hook still refuses unformatted JSON and helper redefinitions in the files it selects, and it never writes the index. One fact for the record: at this head the equal-version guard checks neither packet, because source is 0.4.0. A 0.3.0 packet is held to its trusted release digest and publisher, not to current source. That follows rule 163de663.\n\nSimplification: the head removes 35 alias exports and one dead re-export, and replaces a duplicated pathspec list with one module. No required change.\n\nQualifications that stand: the contention witness uses a TEST signer and scripted acceptance, not a remote scope or HTTP. The browser results are local macOS only, and the notes record the withheld raw views and Grow proofs. No hosted, Linux, provider or physical-device result follows. Hook activation stays with the planner. This approval authorizes no push, landing, signing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:90e1323a3a2884228cffe17b01b386fda2429a0a","binding":"assigned","head":"b3c4b1147e7769b21e97dc9486a99598bef676d6","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e8f14095ab403c3f6487becef2b1c208c721af5f\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:60680427a8544dfea8a1db24d3cd512974bf16d9\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d549e07995dd20b90aaf9171d9dbe77de142bb75\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8d8c4c3f9545d3